00:03:53.200 --> 00:04:01.520
dynamic range because it it shoots alternating&nbsp;
images it it it shoots actually 48 frames&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:08.240
and so one is one exposure and then the other is&nbsp;
an offset exposure and then it alternates and and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:15.680
that offset like if you stop it down two stops it&nbsp;
kind of extends your dynamic range by two stops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:21.680
and then there's a process in post where you can&nbsp;
bring that information back in I don't think I use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:26.560
